course: dictionary
lesson: 4691
title: Feeling words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a feeling, and the words around them show how strong that feeling is. «Homesickness» is the sad feeling of missing your home and family when you are away from them.
explain: Look for the clues. «Suffer from homesickness» tells you the feeling hurts. «A wave of homesickness» tells you it can rush over you suddenly. Ask yourself: what word would fit here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «If you feel homesick, talk to a teacher» still makes sense if homesick means missing home, so you have understood it correctly.
fact: Homesickness is a noun, so it names a feeling.
fact: «Homesickness» means the sad feeling of missing your home and family when you are away.
fact: «Suffer from homesickness» means the feeling makes you unhappy.
fact: «A wave of homesickness» means a sudden rush of this feeling.
fact: Homesickness is common after a move and usually fades over months.
exercise: «She was overcome by a wave of homesickness on her first night away.» What does homesickness mean? | A test at school | Lost in a crowd at the station | *The sad feeling of missing home and family | A love of camping in the woods
exercise: «On a school camp, pack with a parent, label your things and talk to a teacher if you feel homesick.» What does homesick mean? | Excited to meet new friends | Hungry for dinner | Feeling very hot and tired | *Missing your home and family
exercise: «Homesickness is common after a move and usually fades over months.» What does fades suggest? | It gets stronger every day | It stays the same forever | It turns into a game | *It gets weaker and goes away over time
test: «Moving countries is hard for anyone, and homesickness is the ache for the place and people you left.» What is the ache? | A pain in your leg after running | A favourite meal | A new school subject | *A sad longing for the place and people you left
test: Which phrase shows that homesickness can make you unhappy? | Label your things | Pack with a parent | Talk to a teacher | *Suffer from homesickness
exam: Jayden reads «a wave of homesickness» and asks what it means. What is the best answer? | A boat rocking on the sea | A new way of cooking | *A sudden rush of missing home | A loud noise in the hall
